# EduBridge Git Workflow

Full guide: `docs/guides/git-and-release-strategy.md`. Skill: `.agents/skills/edubridge-git/`. Message style aligns with `caveman-commit`.

## Branches

| Branch | Role | Deploy |
|--------|------|--------|
| `main` | Production only | End users |
| `development` | Integration / staging | Test URLs |
| `feature/<short-name>` | One change | PR previews optional |
| `hotfix/<short-name>` | Prod fix from `main` | Then sync into `development` |

Flow: `feature/*` → PR → `development` (test) → PR → `main` (release).

Never push feature work straight to `main`. Do not use `master`.

## When the user asks to commit (or Cursor generates a commit)

1. Confirm branch: feature work on `feature/*` (or `development` only for tiny chore/docs). Never commit product work on `main` unless hotfix.
2. Stage only intended files. Never stage `.env`, secrets, `*.log`, `node_modules`, `.wayfinder/`.
3. Message = Conventional Commits, caveman-commit terse style:
   - `<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>`
   - Types: `feat` `fix` `refactor` `perf` `docs` `test` `chore` `build` `ci` `style` `revert`
   - Scopes (prefer): `web` `agent` `docs` `ui` `ai-ui` `db` `auth` `shell` `student-dashboard` `report-cards` `test-papers` `repo` `ci`
   - Imperative, ≤72 chars subject, no trailing period, no AI attribution fluff
   - Body only for why / breaking / migration / `Closes #N`
4. Only commit when the user explicitly asks. Follow the user rule for git safety (no force push, no amend unless allowed).

## PRs

- Feature → `development`: squash merge preferred.
- `development` → `main`: only after staging verification; clear release summary.
- PR title matches the squash commit subject when possible.

## Changelog

- Dev: update `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` when merging meaningful work to `development` / releasing to `main`.
- User-facing in-app “What’s new” is separate — never dump raw commit subjects into the product UI.
